---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { rel, SUPPORT_EMAIL, LEGAL_NAME } from '../../consts';
const description = `Privacy policy for En Voz Alta, the citizenship interview practice app by ${LEGAL_NAME}: what stays on your iPhone and where Apple is involved.`;
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy · En Voz Alta" description={description} path="/privacy/en-voz-alta" breadcrumbLeaf="En Voz Alta">
  <main class="page">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:720px;">
      <a class="back" href={rel('/privacy/')}>← All privacy policies</a>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">En Voz Alta · Last updated September 28, 2026 · <a href={rel('/privacy/en-voz-alta/es/')} hreflang="es" lang="es">Leer en español</a></p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        En Voz Alta is a practice tool for the U.S. citizenship interview. It has no account, no ads from other companies, no tracking,
        no analytics and no server. Its App Store privacy label is Data Not Collected. This page lists what stays on
        your iPhone and exactly where Apple is involved.
      </p>

      <h2>What stays on this iPhone</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your voice. It is never recorded; speech is processed in memory and discarded.</li>
        <li>What you said, as text. It is erased when the round ends.</li>
        <li>
          Your practice results, your filing date, your optional interview date, your state and the names you typed.
          They are <strong>not included in iCloud Backup</strong>, so they don't move to a new phone.
        </li>
        <li>Your N-400 practice. The app <strong>never saves your yes or no</strong>, or anything you say to those questions.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What this app never has</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No account. No ads from other companies. No tracking, no analytics, no server.</li>
        <li>We never see your answers.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where Apple is involved</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Speech.</strong> This app tells iPhone to recognize speech on the device only. The permission message you see is written by Apple.</li>
        <li><strong>Dictation files.</strong> iPhone downloads English dictation or speech files from Apple. Downloading sends nothing you said.</li>
        <li><strong>Keyboard.</strong> The microphone key on the keyboard is Apple Dictation, under Apple's settings, not this app's. Other companies' keyboards are turned off inside this app.</li>
        <li><strong>Purchases.</strong> Purchases and Restore go through your Apple Account. We see sales totals, never who bought.</li>
        <li><strong>Sharing with developers.</strong> If you turned on "Share with App Developers" in iPhone settings, Apple may send us crash reports and usage totals without your name.</li>
        <li><strong>Reminders.</strong> They are created on this iPhone. No server sends them.</li>
        <li><strong>Links.</strong> Links (uscis.gov, senate.gov, legal-help directories) open in Safari. Those websites see your visit.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>If you email us</h2>
      <p>
        Email opens only when you tap a support link or Report a wrong answer. A wrong-answer report fills in the
        question number, the test version and the app version, and none of your answers. We receive what you choose
        to send, including your email address, and use it only to reply and to fix the app.
      </p>

      <h2>Erasing your data</h2>
      <p>
        In the app, Settings &gt; Erase practice data deletes everything the app stored on this iPhone. Deleting the
        app does the same. Pro stays with your Apple Account and can be restored.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>En Voz Alta is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from them.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes materially, the new version will be posted at this URL with an updated date above.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>

      <p>
        En Voz Alta is a practice tool, not legal advice. Not affiliated with USCIS or any government agency.
        It is made by {LEGAL_NAME}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
